<title>GERMANY: Hoechst says former CFO to head supervisory board.</title>
<headline>Hoechst says former CFO to head supervisory board.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>German chemicals and drugs group Hoechst AG said on Wednesday that Martin Fruehauf, the group's former chief financial officer, had been appointed as head of the group's supervisory board.</p>
<p>Fruehauf, who retired from Hoechst's management board last year, will succeed Erhard Bouillon who has announced he would retire as supervisory board chairman.</p>
<p>-- Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
